    "rationale": "The undiluted readings plateau at about 0.76 from 5 h onward, which suggests the reader has saturated. The retained 18 h aliquot supports this. Diluted 10x, it read 0.264 (replicates 0.261 and 0.267), which is about 2.64 once multiplied back. Diluted 30x, it read 0.090, which is about 2.71. A culture that was truly at 0.75 would read about 0.075 at 10x. The back-calculated value is also still creeping up with dilution (2.64 at 10x, 2.71 at 30x), so some compression remains at 10x. The true OD at 18 h is therefore about 2.7–2.8, roughly 3.5 times the undiluted reading."
